      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynenurii(126TC)/29518",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Type:</strong> Rosulate</li><li><strong>Origin:</strong> Asia</li><li><strong>Growth rate:</strong> Medium</li><li><strong>Height:</strong> 10 - 20+ cm (average height after two months in the tank)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Cryptocorynenurii(126TC)/29518",
      "html": "<p>This beautiful variation of Cryptocoryne nurii was found growing in the wild in Malaysia around 1970. In the aquarium hobby it became popular under the name 'Rose Maiden'.</p><p>The plant is as easy to grow as Cryptocoryne wendtii and has the same size and leaf shape. It will, given the time, produce runners under the bottom layer, often showing up quite far from the mother plant.</p><p>Intensity of colour and patterns in leaves is dependant on light and nutrition.</p>"
    }
